# What a build reader answers: the forge it reads, where a branch points, and what a commit's build did.
# The token comes with each call over the owner-only socket; a reader keeps no secret of its own.
interface org.fuin.porelo.Build2

# Which forge, and which version of this contract the reader speaks.
method Describe() -> (protocolVersion: int, forge: string)

# The commit a branch points at; "" when the forge has no such branch.
method Head(upstream: string, api: string, token: string, branch: string) -> (commit: string)

# One job of a build: the smallest unit the forge reports its own result and its own log for - on GitHub and
# GitLab a job, on Bitbucket a step, on Jenkins a stage with a log of its own or else the whole build. Its name as
# the forge spells it, "<workflow or pipeline> / <job>"; what became of it in lower case, or its state while it is
# not finished; and the last 64 KiB of its log in base64, absent when none is handed over - less when more than 32
# logs share the 2 MiB a build carries in all, each keeping an equal share of its end. A log is always the
# job's plain text: a reader whose forge sends an archive or splits a job into step files unpacks it and joins the
# steps in their order, one header line each, before it takes the end.
type Job (name: string, result: string, log: ?string)

# What the build of one commit did. jobs is every job the forge reports for the commit, in its order, once the
# verdict is "failure" or final - empty while queued or running, and for "unknown" - at most 50. logs says which of
# them carry their log: "none" downloads no log, "failure" each failed job's, "all" every job's once the verdict
# is final; absent, "failure".
method Build(upstream: string, api: string, token: string, commit: string, logs: ?string)
    -> (verdict: string, jobs: []Job, detail: string)

# Opens a pull request from a branch into the repository's default branch, or answers the one already open from it:
# url is where a person reads it, opened whether this call opened it. Absent, the title is the subject of the
# branch's newest commit. A reader that opens none answers org.varlink.service.MethodNotImplemented, as one from
# before this method answers MethodNotFound; Porelo hears both as "this reader cannot".
method OpenPullRequest(upstream: string, api: string, token: string, branch: string, title: ?string)
    -> (url: string, opened: bool)

# The forge limits how often it is asked; retryAfter is in seconds, 0 when it did not say.
error RateLimited(detail: string, retryAfter: int)

# The forge refused the credential: expired, revoked, wrong, or without the scope it needs.
error CredentialRefused(detail: string, retryAfter: int)

# The forge knows no such repository, or the credential may not see it.
error NoSuchRepository(detail: string, retryAfter: int)

# The forge did not answer, or answered something that is not an answer.
error Unreachable(detail: string, retryAfter: int)
